; ..\_01_BSW\Src\PduR\PduR_RmTp.c	   133   *                                In case of gateway the PDU Router module will copy otherwise the source upper layer
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\PduR\PduR_RmTp.c	   134   *                                module will copy the data. If not enough transmit data is available, no data is copied.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\PduR\PduR_RmTp.c	   135   *
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\PduR\PduR_RmTp.c	   136   *                                A copy size of 0 can be used to indicate state changes in the retry parameter.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\PduR\PduR_RmTp.c	   137   *  \param[in]  retry             not supported
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\PduR\PduR_RmTp.c	   138   *  \param[out] availableDataPtr  Indicates the remaining number of bytes that are available in the PduR Tx buffer.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\PduR\PduR_RmTp.c	   139   *                                AvailableTxDataCntPtr can be used by TP modules that support dynamic payload lengths
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\PduR\PduR_RmTp.c	   140   *                                (e.g. Iso FrTp) to determine the size of the following CFs.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\PduR\PduR_RmTp.c	   141   *  \return     BufReq_ReturnType
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\PduR\PduR_RmTp.c	   142   *              BUFREQ_OK         The data has been copied to the transmit buffer successful.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\PduR\PduR_RmTp.c	   143   *              BUFREQ_E_NOT_OK   PduR_Init() has not been called
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\PduR\PduR_RmTp.c	   144   *                                or the GwTpTxPduId is not valid
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\PduR\PduR_RmTp.c	   145   *                                or the GwTpTxPduId is not forwarded in this identity
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\PduR\PduR_RmTp.c	   146   *                                or the info is not valid
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\PduR\PduR_RmTp.c	   147   *                                or the request was not accepted by the upper layer and no data has been copied.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\PduR\PduR_RmTp.c	   148   *              BUFREQ_E_BUSY     The request cannot be processed because the TX data is not available
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\PduR\PduR_RmTp.c	   149   *                                and no data has been copied. The TP layer might retry later the copy process.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\PduR\PduR_RmTp.c	   150   *  \pre         -
